    <DocumentationNarrative Id="source:cli:meta-orchestration:app:narrative:example-example-meta-orchestration-infer-run-plan:infer-and-review-a-run-plan" DocumentationSubjectId="source:cli:meta-orchestration:app" PreviousNarrativeId="source:cli:meta-orchestration:app:narrative:guide:working-with-metaorchestration">
      <Body>Build orchestration from a modeled pipeline, then review the issues and plan.

Inference creates the provable part of the run graph. Any remaining ordering or lock decision is visible in the orchestration workspace before execution.

```powershell
meta-orchestration infer --pipeline-workspace .\Pipeline.Workspace --new-workspace .\Orchestration.Workspace
meta-orchestration list-issues --workspace .\Orchestration.Workspace
meta-orchestration refresh-run-plan --workspace .\Orchestration.Workspace
meta-orchestration inspect-run-plan --workspace .\Orchestration.Workspace
```</Body>
      <Origin>Authored</Origin>
      <ReviewStatus>Current</ReviewStatus>
      <Slot>Example.example:meta-orchestration:infer-run-plan</Slot>
      <Title>Infer and review a run plan</Title>
    </DocumentationNarrative>
    <DocumentationNarrative Id="source:cli:meta-orchestration:app:narrative:guide:working-with-metaorchestration" DocumentationSubjectId="source:cli:meta-orchestration:app" PreviousNarrativeId="source:cli:meta-orchestration:app:narrative:summary:summary">
      <Body>MetaOrchestration turns modeled pipeline tasks and bound transform access evidence into a run graph. It derives the ordering that can be proven from declared reads, writes, and effects, then represents the remaining synchronization choices as explicit policy.

That division is deliberate. Structural evidence can establish a large portion of a safe plan, while dependency rules, lock policies, and concurrent-append decisions supply the operational knowledge that only a designer can provide. The resulting workspace makes both the inferred and authored portions of orchestration visible.

Execution coordinates the modeled run plan and retains run evidence. When an issue remains unresolved, it is recorded as a specific modeled concern rather than disappearing into scheduler code or an implicit ordering convention.</Body>
      <Origin>Authored</Origin>
      <ReviewStatus>Current</ReviewStatus>
      <Slot>Guide</Slot>
      <Title>Working with MetaOrchestration</Title>
